    [Doc][Misc] Sync DeepSeek-V4 flash and Pro deployment documentation fixes to main (#20191)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    This PR synchronizes documentation fixes for DeepSeek-V4 deployment to
    the `main` branch, matching the changes in #20174. Specifically, it:
    - Removes hard-coded `VLLM_PREFIX_CACHE_RETENTION_INTERVAL=4096`
    environment variable exports from both the Flash and Pro deployment
    examples.
    - Removes the parameter description for
    `VLLM_PREFIX_CACHE_RETENTION_INTERVAL` in the key parameter descriptions
    of both tutorials.
    - Revises the prefill context parallelism (PCP) explanation in the Pro
    tutorial (Section 5.1) by removing the introductory standalone-TP
    limitation claim.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. This is a documentation-only update.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Verified the updated Flash tutorial has zero remaining references to
    `VLLM_PREFIX_CACHE_RETENTION_INTERVAL`, including shell exports,
    parameter descriptions and historical-variable guidance.
    - Ran `bash -n` on all affected shell code blocks.
    - Ran `git diff --cached --check`.
    - Ran `bash format.sh ci`.
    - Resolved the Flash parameter-list conflict with current `main`:
    retained `enable_fused_mc2` under `--additional-config` and removed the
    obsolete prefix-retention environment-variable guidance. The Pro file
    merged automatically. Re-ran `git diff --cached --check` and `bash
    format.sh ci` on the merged tree.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
